{"type":"message","id":"fcc56218","parentId":"100eed6e","timestamp":"2026-06-03T13:19:56.100Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read_ts_AY89a18nDwDaYAChFMl06DgUcoxfRD5-dpoQ8Kii0qN6ywTWXGvgpeLRZ-xMOGuUuWNRWUC-Mzw_QNI_0CqE-pwSI2zN-2atK3A3H8hkvKA3FFGvUOB6e__ERVsJV7NudEeWb8V2xaunjJdlObC6karwKDVj-JLEDQmGbJc5qgTUeSFv1zpW8x4xUnzXIkm24Zs-HcVW9dLiYF1ZUwUoFlZX1vBmYE7gP-lV4DWuTNpQNJU7i69p3LpiFyGz0b7Fx2GXSlb9FH6OJ1hqHmUKKdV1eY1DARp5ywrVyF9teia1HdYSHNxmK9E6Hmg8OiYJ2UufVgOHwr7P7IDnx6mNzeAeWv1fxeSA6I1TO68caAHt6ViGbBZQlX8fhx0l1Kx3RXEJRBa_Lqn_1Cl6826F1O1padK29A-mekmuog0e9ilUowd0hhEPScy1dH4H9UKNRRxGj73_rYu6TfYnk-_QLUUxyYNUk8f29ehFUw8yRy2P1NK0EF-9rk_wblswtFlW_VcJK8XUeG9_i02aXr-CiTW24DOKcnrIy4V-_Q-1j9npBzlymCSd2z_xv26qMINVfriYLXNoCKEeEJ38HnfcodhNg2qWDAJeGHbEYFHIRKmpJPgK3ywU72M9rwJ9SIr-VmELaBjAMfK8FWJhaUyeEVAvJOB1BBuFdr0qW8G8fHNiOoJwzBTB1KyWhVWSYxHiaZtSdaLDpxKqxAWBF0czqK8BtoGXR19qR4lYYozwOmlKQR8e_yffWETPtLPuxvLW9bcfrJDAenUU6lQ7CFhr8uIon7108wrtDLn5siM8HW96hpqZ5f9hChi_nBeulbcQwy8mQQn8woBOfXjOUJDDsNXNEovizDiAMP6zptEZYWrRzoZcpBk3sIfbLQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"mode\": \"deep_research\",\n  \"story_id\": \"moonpay-moonagents-desktop-launch\",\n  \"category\": \"adoption_partnership\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"AI and Crypto Integration via Graphical Desktop App\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"MoonAgents MoonPay AI\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"MoonPay Brings Crypto Transactions to Claude and Codex With MoonAgents Desktop App\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Stablecoins\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"tether\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://decrypt.co/369746/moonpay-brings-crypto-transactions-claude-codex-moonagents\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"MoonPay has officially launched the desktop version of its MoonAgents application on Wednesday, June 3, 2026.\",\n    \"The app allows non-technical users to connect Anthropic's Claude Code and OpenAI's Codex to crypto wallets, token swaps, prediction markets, and other decentralized blockchain services via a clean graphical user interface (GUI).\",\n    \"Initially launched in February 2026 as a CLI (command-line interface) tool, this three-month-later desktop launch streamlines setup, allowing users to log in with existing Claude or Codex accounts rather than configuring them manually.\",\n    \"The platform includes prebuilt Skills, scheduled Automations, and an Artifacts system that can automatically generate custom dashboards to manage financial workflows.\",\n    \"Security is maintained by storing fully encrypted private keys locally on the user's computer; the Large Language Models (LLMs) cannot access or view these keys directly, mitigating threats like prompt injections or accidental deletion of data.\",\n    \"This launch follows other AI-related products from MoonPay, including the MoonAgents Card launched in May 2026 which enables AI agents to spend stablecoins anywhere Mastercard is accepted, and a feature letting users purchase crypto through ChatGPT using voice commands.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"#### In brief\\n\\n- MoonPay launched the MoonAgents desktop app, which lets AI assistants interact with crypto wallets and blockchain services.\\n- The software currently works with Claude and OpenAI Codex accounts and is designed to simplify setup for non-technical users.\\n- The app stores wallet keys locally in encrypted form while giving AI assistants access to trading, payments, and other blockchain tools.\\n\\nClaude and ChatGPT can write code—and MoonPay wants to make them trade crypto, too.\\n\\nThe crypto payments company on Wednesday launched the MoonAgents desktop app, a project that allows users to connect Anthropic’s Claude Code and OpenAI’s Codex to crypto wallets, token swaps, prediction markets, and other blockchain services through a visual interface.\\n\\n\\\"All that stuff is hidden under the hood for you,\\\" MoonPay Head of Agents Kevin Arifin told *Decrypt*. “It will set up Codex or Claude locally on your computer behind the scenes, and then it's a front end.”\\n\\nMoonPay first launched MoonAgents in February as a command-line tool. Fast forward three months, and the desktop version moves those capabilities into a graphical interface that handles much of the setup behind the scenes.\\n\\nAccording to Arifin, users can sign in with existing Claude or Codex accounts rather than manually configuring the underlying tools. The software includes prebuilt Skills, scheduled Automations, and an Artifacts system that can generate custom dashboards and other interfaces for managing financial activity.\\n\\nHowever, as AI agents gain more autonomy, concerns about access and oversight have grown.\\n\\nIn April, PocketOS founder Jeremy Crane claimed a Cursor agent running Anthropic’s Claude Opus deleted production data and backups through a single Railway API call, leaving only a three-month-old recoverable backup. Security researchers have also warned about prompt injection attacks, which can trick AI agents into revealing sensitive information or performing actions the user never intended.\\n\\nAccording to Arifin, MoonAgents addresses similar concerns by storing private keys locally, instead of on a cloud server.\\n\\n“The most important piece of security is not revealing the private keys,” he said. “The private keys are stored locally on the user’s computer and are fully encrypted, so the LLM can’t just access or view them. All the keys are stored in such a way that there’s no way for the LLM to see those keys.”\\n\\nThe MoonAgents app is the latest ChatGPT-facing product produced by MoonPay. In May, MoonPay launched a new app that lets users buy cryptocurrencies, including Bitcoin and Solana, through ChatGPT just by speaking with the chatbot.\\n\\nThe biggest use case for the MoonAgents app, Arifin explained, is allowing AI models to run locally on a user's computer, where they can interact with blockchain services using the user's private keys without those credentials being exposed to the AI.\\n\\n\\\"The LLM is not the answer in this case,\\\" Arifin said. \\\"It's empowering you to be able to do the research, dive into the meme coin, dive into the tokens, and dig into the trenches in a way that in the past it was only restricted to the people that could write scripts.\\\"\\n\\nAdditional historical context: In May 2026, MoonPay also announced the MoonAgents Card enabling AI agents to spend stablecoins anywhere Mastercard is accepted. This debit card allows programmatic AI systems to settle payments with stablecoins on networks like Solana, integrating blockchain efficiency with traditional merchants. The desktop app launched on June 3, 2026 serves as the focal GUI control center for configuring these types of agent setups locally, bridging the gap between command-line setups and everyday retail users.\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780492796100}}
